-- title:
--   Minimal primes of a ring with a root of Φ_ℓ
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ and $R$ be commutative rings with $R$ an $A_0$-algebra, and let $\ell$ be a natural number carrying a `Fact` instance that it is prime. Assume the image of $\ell$ in $A_0$ is a unit, that $\omega \in A_0$ is a primitive $\ell$-th root of unity, and that $\omega^i - \omega^j$ is a unit of $A_0$ for all $i, j < \ell$ with $i \neq j$. Let $\xi \in R$ satisfy $\Phi_\ell(\xi) = 0$, where $\Phi_\ell$ is the $\ell$-th cyclotomic polynomial over $A_0$ evaluated at $\xi$ through the algebra map. Two conclusions are asserted. First, every minimal prime $\mathfrak{p}$ of the zero ideal of $R$ contains $\xi - \omega^j$ (image under $A_0 \to R$) for exactly one $j$ with $1 \le j < \ell$. Second, for each $j$ with $1 \le j < \ell$ such that the quotient $R/(\xi - \omega^j)$ is a domain, the principal ideal generated by $\xi - \omega^j$ is itself a minimal prime of the zero ideal, and it is the only minimal prime containing $\xi - \omega^j$.
--
--   This is the commutative-algebra input for splitting a ring carrying a root of $\Phi_\ell$ into its $\ell-1$ cyclotomic branches: the minimal primes are indexed injectively by the nontrivial $\ell$-th roots of unity, and under a domain hypothesis each branch ideal is exactly one of them. It is used in the analysis of the components of modular curves of full level $\ell$, where the minimal primes over the relevant ideal are identified as ideals of the form $(\xi - \omega^j)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Ideal_minimalPrimes_eq_span_sub_pow_of_aeval_cyclotomic_eq_zero.lean

